
Where does FeignClient fit?

Since you're working with Spring Boot microservices, you'll also encounter:

@FeignClient(name = "user-service")
public interface UserClient {

    @GetMapping("/users/{id}")
    User getUser(@PathVariable Long id);
}

Then:

RestTemplate → HTTP client
WebClient    → HTTP client
FeignClient  → Declarative HTTP client

With Feign, you mainly describe the API, rather than manually constructing the HTTP request.

Interview shortcut

Remember:

RestTemplate → old, synchronous/blocking HTTP client
WebClient → modern, supports non-blocking/reactive HTTP communication
FeignClient → declarative client where you define the remote API as an interface.